Package: expectr
Title: Pipeline Checkpoints for Data Expectations
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Daniel", "Madsen", email = "danielmadsen@live.dk",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: State an expectation about data as "the set of violations
    must be empty", build that set with ordinary dplyr, and pass it to a
    checkpoint that warns or aborts with the offending rows. Includes
    checkpoints for unique keys, balanced panels and overlapping spells,
    a tally of many rules at once, and helpers to inspect duplicates and
    column types. Built for full-population registers: in-memory checks
    group keys in one linear pass, and database and Arrow tables are
    checked where they live.
